<pre class=metadata>
Title: JSON Templates
Shortname: json-templates
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/HTML-Additions/json-templates/spec/
Repository: arronei/HTML-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification extends HTML with three content attributes. The <code>json</code>
    attribute on a <{template}> element names a JSON resource for the template to load. The
    <code>template</code> attribute on any HTML element names a template, by its ID, to render into
    that element. The <code>key</code> attribute marks the elements in a template that receive data.
    The user agent makes one copy of the template for each item in the JSON data, and fills in each
    keyed element's text and attributes from the item's property with the same name, without script.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css no
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

